---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Execution Desk · MetaTrader 5"
  description="Connect your own MetaTrader 5 terminal, backtest AI-authored strategies, measure their success rate and route orders from one desk."
>
  <main class="shell ex" data-api="https://trading-llc-mcp.mahdi-t8256.workers.dev">
    <section class="ex-hero">
      <div class="ex-kicker">Execution / MT5 · Section 5.0</div>
      <h1>Execution Desk</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Bridge this website to <b>your own MetaTrader 5 terminal</b>. Backtest a strategy on your
        broker's real history, measure its success rate, then open, manage and close positions from
        here. The bridge runs on your machine and never custodies funds.
      </p>
      <div class="ex-badges">
        <span class="badge ex-badge" id="modeBadge">MODE —</span>
        <span class="badge ex-badge" id="tradeBadge">TRADING —</span>
        <span class="badge ex-badge" id="cloudBadge">CLOUD —</span>
        <a class="badge ex-badge warm" href="/downloads/vaelor-mt5-bridge.zip" download>Download bridge .zip</a>
        <a class="badge ex-badge warm" href="/docs/09-mt5-execution">Setup manual</a>
      </div>

      <div class="ex-quickbar">
        <a href="#connect">Connect</a>
        <a href="#order-ticket">Order ticket</a>
        <a href="#positions">Positions</a>
        <a href="#strategies">Strategies</a>
        <a href="#backtest">Backtest</a>
        <a href="#signals">Signals</a>
        <a href="#audit">Audit</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- status -->
    <section class="ex-statusbar" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="ex-status-left">
        <span class="ex-pulse ex-pulse-off" id="connDot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div>
          <div class="ex-status-title" id="connLabel">BRIDGE OFFLINE</div>
          <div class="ex-status-sub" id="connSub">No local bridge paired yet — follow the three steps below.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ex-status-right">
        <span class="ex-mono" id="lastPoll">poll: —</span>
        <button type="button" class="ex-btn ghost" id="forgetBtn" hidden>Forget pairing</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- setup -->
    <section class="ex-panel" id="connect" aria-labelledby="connect-title">
      <div class="ex-panel-head">
        <div>
          <div class="ex-kicker">Section 01 · Connect your MetaTrader</div>
          <h2 class="ex-title" id="connect-title">CONNECT WIZARD</h2>
        </div>
        <span class="ex-chip" id="setupChip">not paired</span>
      </div>

      <div class="ex-steps">
        <article class="ex-step">
          <span class="ex-step-num">1</span>
          <h3>Download the bridge</h3>
          <p>
            A small package that runs on your PC. It connects to the MetaTrader 5 already installed
            on your machine — no broker API keys, no cloud custody.
          </p>
          <a class="ex-btn primary" href="/downloads/vaelor-mt5-bridge.zip" download>
            Download vaelor-mt5-bridge.zip
          </a>
        </article>
        <article class="ex-step">
          <span class="ex-step-num">2</span>
          <h3>Run it once</h3>
          <p>
            Unzip, then double-click <code>run.cmd</code>. The first run creates a private Python
            environment and installs dependencies. The console prints a URL and a token.
          </p>
          <pre class="ex-code">URL   : http://127.0.0.1:8899
Token : &lt;random string&gt;</pre>
        </article>
        <article class="ex-step">
          <span class="ex-step-num">3</span>
          <h3>Paste URL + token</h3>
          <p>
            Pair the site with your bridge. The token stays in this browser only; it is never sent
            to our servers.
          </p>
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="bridgeUrl">Bridge URL</label>
            <input id="bridgeUrl" type="url" inputmode="url" spellcheck="false" placeholder="http://127.0.0.1:8899" />
          </div>
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="bridgeToken">Bridge token</label>
            <input id="bridgeToken" type="password" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" placeholder="paste the token printed by the bridge" />
          </div>
          <div class="ex-btn-row">
            <button type="button" class="ex-btn primary" id="connectBtn">Connect</button>
            <button type="button" class="ex-btn ghost" id="testBtn">Test connection</button>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="ex-note">
        <b>Any Windows PC works.</b> The bridge auto-detects every MetaTrader 5 terminal installed
        for your user, including broker-branded and portable copies. If none is logged in yet, open
        MetaTrader 5, sign in to a demo or live account, then connect again.
      </div>

      <div class="ex-diag" id="diagWrap" hidden>
        <div class="ex-diag-head">
          <div>
            <div class="ex-kicker">Detected on this machine</div>
            <div class="ex-diag-title" id="diagSummary">Scanning terminals…</div>
          </div>
          <div class="ex-head-actions">
            <button type="button" class="ex-btn ghost" id="disconnectBtn" hidden>Disconnect terminal</button>
            <button type="button" class="ex-btn ghost" id="rescanBtn">Rescan</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ex-table-wrap">
          <table class="ex-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Terminal</th>
                <th>Status</th>
                <th>Account path</th>
                <th class="right">Action</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="terminalList">
              <tr><td colspan="4" class="ex-empty">No bridge paired yet.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <details class="ex-details">
          <summary>Terminal is installed but not logged in? Optional sign-in</summary>
          <p class="ex-hint">
            These values are used for a single <code>mt5.initialize</code> call and immediately
            discarded. They are never written to disk, the audit log or the cloud. Prefer logging in
            inside MetaTrader 5 itself.
          </p>
          <div class="ex-grid-3">
            <div class="ex-field">
              <label for="loginLogin">Login</label>
              <input id="loginLogin" type="number" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="600143124" />
            </div>
            <div class="ex-field">
              <label for="loginServer">Server</label>
              <input id="loginServer" type="text" placeholder="Opogroup-Server1" spellcheck="false" />
            </div>
            <div class="ex-field">
              <label for="loginPassword">Password</label>
              <input id="loginPassword" type="password" autocomplete="off" placeholder="not stored" />
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ex-btn-row">
            <button type="button" class="ex-btn" id="manualConnectBtn">Sign in &amp; connect</button>
          </div>
        </details>

        <div class="ex-callout warn" id="autotradingNote" hidden>
          <b>AutoTrading is off in the terminal.</b>
          Reading prices, positions and history still works. To send real orders, press the
          <b>AutoTrading</b> button in MetaTrader 5 and enable
          <b>Tools &gt; Options &gt; Expert Advisors &gt; Allow algorithmic trading</b>.
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- account -->
    <section class="ex-panel" id="accountPanel" hidden aria-labelledby="account-title">
      <div class="ex-panel-head">
        <div>
          <div class="ex-kicker">Section 02 · Connected account</div>
          <h2 class="ex-title" id="account-title">ACCOUNT &amp; RISK STRIP</h2>
        </div>
        <span class="ex-chip" id="acctMode">—</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ex-acct-grid">
        <div class="ex-acct-cell"><span>Login</span><b id="acctLogin">—</b></div>
        <div class="ex-acct-cell"><span>Server</span><b id="acctServer">—</b></div>
        <div class="ex-acct-cell"><span>Company</span><b id="acctCompany">—</b></div>
        <div class="ex-acct-cell"><span>Owner</span><b id="acctName">—</b></div>
        <div class="ex-acct-cell"><span>Balance</span><b id="acctBalance">—</b></div>
        <div class="ex-acct-cell"><span>Equity</span><b id="acctEquity">—</b></div>
        <div class="ex-acct-cell"><span>Free margin</span><b id="acctFree">—</b></div>
        <div class="ex-acct-cell"><span>Floating P/L</span><b id="acctProfit">—</b></div>
        <div class="ex-acct-cell"><span>Leverage</span><b id="acctLeverage">—</b></div>
        <div class="ex-acct-cell"><span>AutoTrading</span><b id="acctAutotrading">—</b></div>
      </div>
      <p class="ex-hint" id="accountNote"></p>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- order + risk -->
    <div class="ex-grid-2" id="order-ticket">
      <section class="ex-panel" aria-labelledby="ticket-title">
        <div class="ex-panel-head">
          <div>
            <div class="ex-kicker">Section 03 · Manual routing</div>
            <h2 class="ex-title" id="ticket-title">ORDER TICKET</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="ex-chip" id="ticketChip">simulation</span>
        </div>

        <div class="ex-quote" id="orderQuote">
          <span><i>bid</i><b id="qBid">—</b></span>
          <span><i>ask</i><b id="qAsk">—</b></span>
          <span><i>spread</i><b id="qSpread">—</b></span>
          <span><i>day</i><b id="qChange">—</b></span>
        </div>

        <div class="ex-field">
          <label for="orderSymbol">Symbol</label>
          <select id="orderSymbol"></select>
        </div>

        <div class="ex-side" role="group" aria-label="Order side">
          <button type="button" class="ex-side-btn buy active" id="sideBuy" data-side="buy">BUY</button>
          <button type="button" class="ex-side-btn sell" id="sideSell" data-side="sell">SELL</button>
        </div>

        <div class="ex-grid-3">
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="orderVolume">Volume (lots)</label>
            <input id="orderVolume" type="number" min="0.01" step="0.01" value="0.01" />
          </div>
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="orderSl">Stop loss</label>
            <input id="orderSl" type="number" step="any" placeholder="optional" />
          </div>
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="orderTp">Take profit</label>
            <input id="orderTp" type="number" step="any" placeholder="optional" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ex-grid-2-tight">
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="orderStrategy">Attach to strategy (optional)</label>
            <select id="orderStrategy"><option value="">manual trade</option></select>
          </div>
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="orderComment">Comment</label>
            <input id="orderComment" type="text" maxlength="64" placeholder="execution desk" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <label class="ex-check">
          <input type="checkbox" id="orderConfirm" />
          <span>I confirm this order goes to <b>my broker account</b>.</span>
        </label>

        <div class="ex-btn-row">
          <button type="button" class="ex-btn primary" id="placeOrderBtn">Place order</button>
          <button type="button" class="ex-btn ghost" id="beModeBtn" hidden>Live interlock</button>
        </div>
        <p class="ex-hint" id="orderHint">
          Simulation fills are labelled. Real orders require a connected terminal,
          <code>ALLOW_LIVE_TRADES=1</code> and a typed confirmation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ex-panel" aria-labelledby="risk-title">
        <div class="ex-panel-head">
          <div>
            <div class="ex-kicker">Section 04 · Safety</div>
            <h2 class="ex-title" id="risk-title">RISK GATES &amp; KILL SWITCH</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="ex-chip" id="killChip">armed</span>
        </div>

        <div class="ex-grid-3">
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="riskPerTrade">Risk per trade %</label>
            <input id="riskPerTrade" type="number" min="0.05" max="5" step="0.05" />
          </div>
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="riskMaxLot">Max lots / trade</label>
            <input id="riskMaxLot" type="number" min="0.01" max="100" step="0.01" />
          </div>
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="riskMaxPositions">Max open positions</label>
            <input id="riskMaxPositions" type="number" min="1" max="50" step="1" />
          </div>
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="riskMaxDailyLoss">Max daily loss %</label>
            <input id="riskMaxDailyLoss" type="number" min="0.5" max="50" step="0.5" />
          </div>
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="riskMaxDD">Max drawdown %</label>
            <input id="riskMaxDD" type="number" min="1" max="100" step="1" />
          </div>
          <div class="ex-field">
            <label for="riskWhitelist">Symbol whitelist</label>
            <input id="riskWhitelist" type="text" placeholder="empty = all symbols" spellcheck="false" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <label class="ex-check">
          <input type="checkbox" id="riskAllowMarket" />
          <span>Allow market orders (uncheck to limit the desk to limit orders)</span>
        </label>

        <div class="ex-btn-row">
          <button type="button" class="ex-btn" id="saveRiskBtn">Save risk gates</button>
        </div>

        <hr class="ex-rule" />

        <p class="ex-hint">
          The kill switch blocks every new order immediately. It can also flatten the book.
          Turning it off is deliberately a separate, explicit action.
        </p>
        <label class="ex-check">
          <input type="checkbox" id="killClose" />
          <span>Also close every open position</span>
        </label>
        <div class="ex-btn-row">
          <button type="button" class="ex-btn danger" id="killBtn">Engage kill switch</button>
          <button type="button" class="ex-btn ghost" id="releaseKillBtn" hidden>Release kill switch</button>
        </div>
        <p class="ex-hint" id="killState">Kill switch is off.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- positions -->
    <section class="ex-panel" id="positions" aria-labelledby="pos-title">
      <div class="ex-panel-head">
        <div>
          <div class="ex-kicker">Section 05 · Live book</div>
          <h2 class="ex-title" id="pos-title">POSITIONS &amp; PENDING ORDERS</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-head-actions">
          <span class="ex-chip" id="posCount">0 positions</span>
          <label class="ex-inline">
            <span>Trail pips</span>
            <input id="trailPips" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="30" />
          </label>
          <button type="button" class="ex-btn danger ghost" id="closeAllBtn">Close all</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ex-table-wrap">
        <table class="ex-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Ticket</th>
              <th>Symbol</th>
              <th>Side</th>
              <th class="right">Volume</th>
              <th class="right">Open</th>
              <th class="right">Current</th>
              <th class="right">SL</th>
              <th class="right">TP</th>
              <th class="right">P/L</th>
              <th>Strategy</th>
              <th class="right">Actions</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="positionsBody">
            <tr><td colspan="11" class="ex-empty">No positions. Connect a terminal to see your live book.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <details class="ex-details" id="ordersWrap">
        <summary>Pending orders (<span id="ordersCount">0</span>)</summary>
        <div class="ex-table-wrap">
          <table class="ex-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Ticket</th>
                <th>Symbol</th>
                <th>Side</th>
                <th>Type</th>
                <th class="right">Volume</th>
                <th class="right">Price</th>
                <th class="right">SL</th>
                <th class="right">TP</th>
                <th>Strategy</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="ordersBody">
              <tr><td colspan="9" class="ex-empty">No pending orders.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- strategies -->
    <section class="ex-panel" id="strategies" aria-labelledby="strat-title">
      <div class="ex-panel-head">
        <div>
          <div class="ex-kicker">Section 06 · Human and AI strategies</div>
          <h2 class="ex-title" id="strat-title">STRATEGY REGISTRY</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-head-actions">
          <span class="ex-chip" id="cloudState">cloud —</span>
          <button type="button" class="ex-btn ghost" id="syncStrategiesBtn">Sync from cloud</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="ex-hint">
        Strategies published through the AI/MCP bridge arrive <b>disabled</b>. Enable one here to let
        it trigger, or enable auto-execute to let it route fresh signals unattended. The kill switch
        always overrides.
      </p>
      <div class="ex-table-wrap">
        <table class="ex-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Strategy</th>
              <th>Source</th>
              <th>Evidence</th>
              <th class="right">Trades</th>
              <th class="right">Success</th>
              <th class="right">Score</th>
              <th class="center">Enabled</th>
              <th class="center">Auto-exec</th>
              <th class="right">Action</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="strategiesBody">
            <tr><td colspan="9" class="ex-empty">No strategies registered yet.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- backtest + performance -->
    <section class="ex-panel" id="backtest" aria-labelledby="bt-title">
      <div class="ex-panel-head">
        <div>
          <div class="ex-kicker">Section 07 · Evidence</div>
          <h2 class="ex-title" id="bt-title">BACKTEST ON BROKER HISTORY</h2>
        </div>
        <span class="ex-chip" id="btChip">event-driven</span>
      </div>

      <div class="ex-grid-4">
        <div class="ex-field">
          <label for="btStrategy">Strategy</label>
          <select id="btStrategy"></select>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-field">
          <label for="btSymbol">Symbol</label>
          <input id="btSymbol" type="text" value="XAUUSD" spellcheck="false" />
        </div>
        <div class="ex-field">
          <label for="btTimeframe">Timeframe</label>
          <select id="btTimeframe">
            <option>M5</option><option>M15</option><option>M30</option>
            <option selected>H1</option><option>H4</option><option>D1</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-field">
          <label for="btBalance">Initial balance</label>
          <input id="btBalance" type="number" min="101" step="100" value="10000" />
        </div>
        <div class="ex-field">
          <label for="btRisk">Risk %</label>
          <input id="btRisk" type="number" min="0.05" max="10" step="0.05" placeholder="strategy default" />
        </div>
        <div class="ex-field">
          <label for="btSpread">Spread (pips)</label>
          <input id="btSpread" type="number" min="0" step="0.1" value="2" />
        </div>
        <div class="ex-field">
          <label for="btCommission">Commission / lot</label>
          <input id="btCommission" type="number" min="0" step="0.5" value="0" />
        </div>
        <div class="ex-field">
          <label for="btLeverage">Leverage cap</label>
          <input id="btLeverage" type="number" min="1" max="1000" step="1" value="100" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ex-btn-row">
        <button type="button" class="ex-btn primary" id="runBacktestBtn">Run backtest</button>
        <span class="ex-mono" id="btStatus">pick a strategy and run it on your broker's history</span>
      </div>

      <div id="btResult" hidden>
        <div class="ex-stat-grid" id="btStats"></div>
        <div class="ex-chart-wrap">
          <div class="ex-chart-head">
            <span>Equity curve</span>
            <span class="ex-mono" id="btMeta"></span>
          </div>
          <canvas id="btCanvas" height="240" aria-label="Backtest equity curve"></canvas>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-table-wrap">
          <table class="ex-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>#</th>
                <th>Opened</th>
                <th>Side</th>
                <th class="right">Entry</th>
                <th class="right">Exit</th>
                <th class="right">P/L</th>
                <th class="right">R</th>
                <th class="right">Bars</th>
                <th>Exit reason</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="btTradesBody"></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="ex-hint">
          Results are evidence, not a promise. A high win rate on a small sample is marked
          <b>insufficient</b> or <b>low</b> confidence on purpose.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ex-panel" aria-labelledby="perf-title">
      <div class="ex-panel-head">
        <div>
          <div class="ex-kicker">Section 08 · Measured results</div>
          <h2 class="ex-title" id="perf-title">SUCCESS RATE</h2>
        </div>
        <span class="ex-chip" id="perfChip">—</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ex-table-wrap">
        <table class="ex-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Strategy</th>
              <th>Evidence</th>
              <th class="right">Trades</th>
              <th class="right">Win rate</th>
              <th class="right">Profit factor</th>
              <th class="right">Expectancy R</th>
              <th class="right">Max DD</th>
              <th class="right">Score</th>
              <th>Confidence</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="perfBody">
            <tr><td colspan="9" class="ex-empty">No measured results yet — run a backtest.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="ex-hint" id="perfNote"></p>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- signals -->
    <section class="ex-panel" id="signals" aria-labelledby="sig-title">
      <div class="ex-panel-head">
        <div>
          <div class="ex-kicker">Section 09 · AI signal queue</div>
          <h2 class="ex-title" id="sig-title">SIGNAL QUEUE</h2>
        </div>
        <span class="ex-chip" id="signalCount">0 pending</span>
      </div>
      <p class="ex-hint">
        Signals created by people or AI through MCP land here as <b>pending</b>. Approving sends a
        market order through the risk gates; rejecting records the decision back to the cloud so the
        author sees the outcome.
      </p>
      <div class="ex-table-wrap">
        <table class="ex-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Received</th>
              <th>Strategy</th>
              <th>Symbol</th>
              <th>Side</th>
              <th class="right">Entry</th>
              <th class="right">SL</th>
              <th class="right">TP</th>
              <th class="right">Conf.</th>
              <th>Note</th>
              <th class="right">Decision</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="signalsBody">
            <tr><td colspan="10" class="ex-empty">No pending signals.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- audit -->
    <section class="ex-panel" id="audit" aria-labelledby="audit-title">
      <div class="ex-panel-head">
        <div>
          <div class="ex-kicker">Section 10 · Traceability</div>
          <h2 class="ex-title" id="audit-title">AUDIT LOG</h2>
        </div>
        <span class="ex-chip" id="auditCount">—</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ex-table-wrap ex-audit-wrap">
        <table class="ex-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Time</th><th>Actor</th><th>Action</th><th>Detail</th><th>Status</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="auditBody">
            <tr><td colspan="5" class="ex-empty">Nothing logged yet.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ex-panel ex-about">
      <div class="ex-panel-head">
        <div>
